# Optional. You almost certainly do NOT need this file.
#
# The app calls /otp/... on its own origin in both environments, and that path is proxied
# to the routing engine:
#
#   npm run dev  — proxied by the server.proxy rule in vite.config.ts
#   deployed     — proxied by Netlify, via public/_redirects
#
# Both read the same address from public/_redirects, so there is one place to change if
# the routing engine moves, and no environment variable to configure on Netlify.
#
# Set VITE_OTP_BASE_URL only to bypass that and call an engine directly — for example an
# OTP you are running locally while the shared one is down:
#
#   VITE_OTP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
#
# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored) to do so. Vite inlines VITE_* variables when
# the dev server starts and when a build runs, so restart `npm run dev` after changing it.
# Editing it while the server is running has no effect.

# Epic 7 reliability API. Leave unset for the Vite development proxy, or set this to the
# deployed FastAPI origin. The API will return an explicit unsupported result until a
# service has passed the historical-data and chronological-evaluation gates.
# VITE_RELIABILITY_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
